/*
 * SPDX-FileCopyrightText: nirapod-sha2 contributors
 * SPDX-FileCopyrightText: nirapod-sha2 contributors
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * sha512_x4_compress.jinc (x86-64, avx2)
 * ======================================
 *
 * Four independent SHA-512 compressions in AVX2, with the entry points and
 * contracts of the scalar 4-way kernel (src/sha512_x4_compress.jinc):
 *
 *     _sha512_x4_compress(h4, blocks, ms)
 *     _sha512_x4_compress_lanes(h4, in, off, n, ms)
 *
 * Lane layout: one 256-bit register holds the same word of the four
 * instances, qword k for instance k, so state register j is h4[:u256 j].
 * Each quarter block (four words) of the four instances is a 4 x 4 matrix
 * of qwords, transposed by VPUNPCK{L,H}_4u64 and VPERM2I128 and made
 * big-endian by VPSHUFB (FIPS 180-4 section 3.1). Both entry points
 * transpose into a 16-word schedule window on the stack, _compress from
 * the block array and _compress_lanes straight from lane memory, and run
 * _sha512_x4_block on it.
 *
 * Rounds (_sha512_x4_block): rounds 0 to 15 are unrolled, rounds 16 to 79
 * are a loop of four passes over 16 unrolled rounds, a third of the code of
 * a full unroll, which made one-block calls slower (docs/KERNELS.md); after
 * 16 rounds the state rotation and the window are back in place. AVX2 has no
 * 64-bit rotate, so ROTR by r is a right shift, a left shift by 64 - r and
 * an XOR, except ROTR 8 in sigma0, which is a byte shuffle. Further savings
 * per round:
 *
 *     K_t is read from a table holding it four times, as the memory
 *     operand of the addition, instead of being broadcast
 *     Maj(a, b, c) = ((a ^ b) & (b ^ c)) ^ b, where b ^ c is the a ^ b of
 *     the round before, so Maj costs three operations
 *     T1 is accumulated in the register of h, whose old value is dead,
 *     with W_t + K_t, Ch and h added before Sigma1(e), so that e' = d + T1
 *     waits only for Sigma1
 *
 * Required CPU feature: AVX2.
 *
 * Security: h4 and the blocks are secret. Every address is fixed at
 * compile time or derived from the public round counter and the public
 * lane pointers. Residue: the local schedule window holds 16 schedule
 * words of every instance on return, W_64 .. W_79; clearing is the
 * export's obligation.
 */

/*
 * SHA-512 constants K_0 .. K_79 (FIPS 180-4 section 4.2.3), each repeated
